Initialize
1.	Set head, tail, and current to NULL.
2.	Display the menu and read the user's choice.

Add Song
3.	Read title, artist, and album; create a new node.
4.	If empty, set head, tail, and current to the new node.
5.	Otherwise link the new node after tail and update tail.

Display Playlist
6.	If head is NULL, report an empty playlist.
7.	Otherwise traverse from head using next and print every song.

Play Current / Next / Previous
8.	If current is NULL, report an empty playlist.
9.	For Next, move current to current->next if it exists.
10.	For Previous, move current to current->prev if it exists.
11.	Display the selected song details.

Search Song
12.	Read a title and traverse from head.
13.	If a matching title is found, display its details; otherwise report not found.

Delete Song
14.	Find the node with the requested title.
15.	Reconnect neighbouring nodes and update head or tail when necessary.
16.	If current is deleted, select the next node if available, otherwise the previous node.

17.	Delete the node.
Reverse Playlist
18.	For every node, swap prev and next.
19.	Swap head and tail.

Clear Playlist
20.	Traverse the list and delete every node, saving next before deletion.
21.	Set head, tail, and current to NULL.

Exit
22.	Repeat until the user enters 0.
23.	The destructor releases any remaining nodes.

